<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish bus strike averted as minister intervenes.</title>
<headline>Irish bus strike averted as minister intervenes.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>A nationwide public transport strike, due to start on Tuesday, was averted after last minute intervention by minister for public transport Mary O'Rourke late on Monday.</p>
<p>O'Rourke called on national transport group Bus Eireann to defer the introduction of 20 new minibus routes in Cork, Galway, Limerick and Waterford today and trade unions responded by cancelling their strike plans.</p>
<p>The transport minister said she would now be meeting both management and unions as soon as possible and would brief the cabinet on the situation later today.</p>
<p>-- Dublin newsroom + 353 1 676 9775</p>
</text>
